                <pb facs="0147" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg63"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Referring to his telegram of May 30, Mr. Conger reports that the Russian
                    minister says he has not yet received instructions and can not make definite
                    statement on the question without them. The Russian minister thinks reply as to
                    cooperation has been sent from St. Petersburg to the Department of State.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
